message:
A Core Sync run finished with at least one phase error. Core Sync writes this JSON log from `recordCoreSyncRunResult` whenever any phase's `errors` count is above zero, which is also the condition that blocks Watch catalog publication for that run (see `src/services/watch-catalog-publication.ts`).

Inspect `/dashboard/workflows` for the failing `core-sync` run's `failedPhases` and `totals`, and check admin logs for `core-sync.*.page.error` lines around the same time to find the underlying Core GraphQL failure. A re-run is safe and idempotent; soft-delete only fires on a clean full run, so a partial run never decimates the catalogue on its own.

